omium:653183 BRANCH=none TEST=make buildall. Run cts.py -m i2c for 100kHz with 10k ohms pull-up registers on SCL and SDA. TH=stm32l476g-eval DUT=nucleo-f072rb.  Change-Id: I8121b1c5dc7542da45141543e35036ef41364c38 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/393331 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="393331" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/31/393331/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I765004292d357a3162964abbde0ec61f6070b326" commit="2f36179026f742f456fff296c91144499997d1cf" commit_message="rotor: Adding new board rotor  This patch adds rotor as a board option. It includes the base files needed to build rotor. In order to unblock further development a SPI flash is included despite rotor not needing it.  BUG=None TEST=emerge sys-boot/depthcharge BRANCH=None  Change-Id: I765004292d357a3162964abbde0ec61f6070b326 Signed-off-by: Calvin Odell &lt;codell@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/363587 Commit-Ready: Peter Tucker &lt;ptucker@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="363587" owner_email="codell@marvell.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/87/363587/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I58228c16a66dc362c91c67aea9f837a10c4f2901" commit="faabb3c9d8561c0612dedeaedec31e628fe73820" commit_message="gpio: rotor: Adding init gpio support  Added gpio driver support for rotor in depthcharge. FLAG_LIDSW, and FLAG_PWRSW are both needed to unblock further development we have included stub implementations until more information about the hardware is available.  BUG=None TEST=emerge-rotor sys-boot/depthcharge BRANCH=None  Change-Id: I58228c16a66dc362c91c67aea9f837a10c4f2901 Signed-off-by: Calvin Odell &lt;codell@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/364789 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="364789" owner_email="codell@marvell.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/89/364789/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0ccb2ad6972704cf101ebdbcad91863603c97c2d" commit="245ffeaf869e02e59d6d0edb1bde4eea20970e0b" commit_message="storage: rotor: Adding SD/eMMC initial support  Rotor can boot to kernel from SD card. This implementation is currently for SD only. To boot from the SD card it has been declared as a fixed_block_device. This will be addressed later  BUG=None TEST=emerge-rotor sys-boot/depthcharge, boot to kernel. BRANCH=None  Change-Id: I0ccb2ad6972704cf101ebdbcad91863603c97c2d Signed-off-by: Calvin Odell &lt;codell@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/364790 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="364790" owner_email="codell@marvell.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/90/364790/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I19825a7c8c4f9bda2a9c74d48d7cec0d05792f9a" commit="cb31eff0763c12f48fb691341def300d2bd51cf7" commit_message="config_lib: Remove _template setting through apply().  apply() will no longer update _template in any case. Update other config_lib methods to have explicit _template value handling. Remove all remaining references to _template from chromeos_config.  Also, removed a bunch of unneccesary overwrite values. Some of the overwrite values now come build board configs, so there is no need to overwrite them.  Include the assert that detected these as commented out code as a reminder to add an appropriate unittest later on. This test is useful, but I don't want to run it every time, otherwise auto-updated values might hit asserts when they are good changes to accept.  Get rid of unused method definitions, and local variables. Get rid of local BuildConfig instances. Use apply instead of derive in a variety of places. Use arguments in apply, instead of creating single use templates.  BUG=chromium:645296 TEST=run_tests, no config_dump.json changes.  Change-Id: I19825a7c8c4f9bda2a9c74d48d7cec0d05792f9a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388904 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="388904" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/04/388904/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iadc11b0edbaab07e850660a2e47cd6a82eab2c71" commit="6afd4f031ade3db5e70e9e64c8a98520210b2199" commit_message="chromeos_config: Create ApplyCustomOverrides method.  Move special build overrides out into a standalone method.  BUG=chromium:645296 TEST=run_tests, no config_dump.json changes.  Change-Id: Iadc11b0edbaab07e850660a2e47cd6a82eab2c71 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390382 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390382" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/82/390382/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2f6638725b42bf4d0f2f184939f8f1bf72b68e39" commit="5ef59c041c3403534219545327f9084ff8fa70cb" commit_message="chromeos_config: Setup beaglebone board configs.  This adds most beaglebone special handling into a board specific values. This affects the config_dump.json quite a bit, but only for builds that were unused and look like they never could have been built.  When looking at the config_dump, these are the only configs in real use.   beaglebone-paladin   beaglebone-release   beaglebone_servo-release  BUG=chromium:645296 TEST=run_tests, no config_dump.json changes.  Change-Id: I2f6638725b42bf4d0f2f184939f8f1bf72b68e39 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390383 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390383" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/83/390383/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ie3654cd1c1cb76b62aa9b247879b60cbecee0155" commit="9f49a716295585f2f2e0e3303488f83ec4ce0390" commit_message="rockchip/rk3399: Add Type-C PHY init  Though we don't use Type-C PHY to support USB3 in firmware, we still need to initialize the Type-C PHY, and make sure the power state of pipe is always fixed to U2/P2. After this, we can force USB3 controller to work in USB2 only mode stability.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:56425 TEST=Go to recovery mode, plug a Type-C USB drive containing chrome OS image into both ports in all orientations, check if system can boot form USB.  Change-Id: Ie3654cd1c1cb76b62aa9b247879b60cbecee0155 Signed-off-by: William wu &lt;wulf@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/391412 Commit-Ready: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="391412" owner_email="wulf@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/12/391412/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id4724935fe9e5352feea4cc535d6c5a52acd2dc9" commit="58aedb06c1aaa9334040f8bf560b6efc8c57997b" commit_message="power_manager: Add [S,G]etBacklightsForcedOff constants.  Add constants for new SetBacklightsForcedOff and GetBacklightsForcedOff D-Bus methods that will be exported by powerd.  BUG=chromium:651669 TEST=built it  Change-Id: Id4724935fe9e5352feea4cc535d6c5a52acd2dc9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394146 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Qiang Xu &lt;warx@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394146" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/system_api" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/system_api" ref="refs/changes/46/394146/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I00cb325b9938e4276cc77b5d6f5faa7023379608" commit="942bdffb307e373f96c127714e0d47cc44c97d67" commit_message="gru: Add USB 2.0 PHY tuning for Kevin PHY0 and PHY1  We found that Kevin board PHY0 and PHY1 eye-diagram margin is not enough to make compliance test pass, and the PHY0 USB SI is worse than PHY1, because of the higher PCB impedance.  For PHY0, we can't improve the eye-diagram by SW PHY tuning, so we need to reduce the RBIAS resistance from 133 ohm to 115 ohm, it can help to increase the eye-height.  For PHY1, we can improve the eye-diagram by setting the max pre-emphasis level.  And after the above change, the USB2 signal amplitude will become larger at the test point near to SOC USB2 PHY, in order to avoid mis-trigger the disconnect detection (650mV), we need to disable pre-emphasize in eop state.  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:53863 TEST=do USB 2.0 compliance test for Kevin C0 and C1 port.  Change-Id: I00cb325b9938e4276cc77b5d6f5faa7023379608 Signed-off-by: William wu &lt;wulf@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390615 Commit-Ready: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390615" owner_email="wulf@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/15/390615/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9161cb7fd902e1f99c7990522fbf72d48cf1dee8" commit="3f1d88713910fabe055f2e4a38b3acd4cf297464" commit_message="use /run instead of /var/run  /var/run is a symlink to /run, so use paths under /run directly. This also makes things more robust in case /var/ is corrupted.  BUG=None TEST=precq passes  Change-Id: I9161cb7fd902e1f99c7990522fbf72d48cf1dee8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394186 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394186" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chrom